  {
    "name": "documents.search",
    "description": "Hybrid (BM25 + vector) search over ingested and knowledge documents. Semantic: finds docs about a concept even without exact word overlap. Honors since/source/author filters. Returns ranked, VFS-citable results."
  },
  {
    "name": "documents.ls",
    "description": "List children of the knowledge VFS. args: path \u2014 start at 'knowledge/documents' (one dir per ingested document) or 'knowledge/conversations'. Returns entries [{name, type, path}]."
  },
  {
    "name": "documents.cat",
    "description": "Read a document's FULL text as line-numbered lines (L1: \u2026, L2: \u2026) for precise citation. args: path \u2014 e.g. 'knowledge/documents/<id>/content.lines' using an id from documents.ls or a path from documents.grep."
  },
  {
    "name": "documents.read",
    "description": "Read a BOUNDED region of any leaf, with paging metadata (start_line/end_line/total_lines/next_start/complete). USE THIS for long email threads, large workbooks, long PDFs and any file whose size you do not know: read a window, then follow next_start. Prefer it over documents.cat, which returns the whole artifact and can exhaust your context. args: path, start_line (1-based), max_lines."
  },
  {
    "name": "documents.grep",
    "description": "Regex-search ALL knowledge content (documents and conversations). args: pattern (regex, case-insensitive), path_prefix ('knowledge'). Returns matches [{path, line, snippet}] \u2014 read a hit's full text with documents.cat(path=path + '/content.lines')."
  },
  {
    "name": "ingest_knowledge_from_text",
    "description": "Extract structured knowledge (entities/relationships) from text and store it in Atom's memory and knowledge graph"
  },
  {
    "name": "save_business_fact",
    "description": "Store a verifiable business fact with citations. Use this for Truths (policies, rules), not just observations."
  },
  {
    "name": "verify_citation",
    "description": "Check if a citation (file path) is valid and read it to confirm the fact."
  },
  {
    "name": "get_system_health",
    "description": "Query the health, performance, and drift of integrated services"
  },
  {
    "name": "request_human_intervention",
    "description": "Explicitly pause execution to ask a human for approval or clarification on a sensitive action"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp_tool_search",
    "description": "Search for more capabilities/tools if you can't find what you need in the current list. Returns list of tools that you can then use in the NEXT step."
  }
]

FORMAT: You must respond with structured output containing:
- thought: Your reasoning about what to do next
- action: If you need to use a SINGLE tool, provide {"tool": "tool_name", "params": {...}}
- actions: If you need to use MULTIPLE INDEPENDENT tools at once, provide [{"tool": "tool_name", "params": {...}}, ...]. Only use this when the tools do NOT depend on each other's output — they run in parallel.
- final_answer: If you have enough information to answer, provide the response
- information_wait: If one required fact/record is missing and cannot be obtained with an available tool, provide {"question": "the specific question", "missing_fact": "the one fact you need", "subject": "optional business subject"}. This durably pauses THIS run and resumes the same work when an authorized answer arrives. Do NOT use this for permission/approval to perform an action; use the normal approval path for that.

Only provide EITHER action OR actions OR final_answer OR information_wait, not multiple.

